  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Chlorofluorocarbon compounds (CFCs)&nbsp;are non-reactive, non-flammable molecules that are used in refrigerators, air conditioners, plastics, and electronic industries. Once released CFCs mix with atmospheric gases and reach the stratosphere, where they are decomposed by UV radiations.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>uv</mi></mover><mover><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>The chlorine radical released will react with ozone.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mrow><mi>ClO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover></math></p><p>The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;will generate chlorine radicals again</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>ClO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8857;</mo></mover></math></p></blockquote>",
